Friday, July 4th from 19:00 till 22:00  
Location: Tkkrlab, Marssteden 98, Enschede  
Max. 10 participants – [Reserve your spot](https://tickets.tkkrlab.space/TkkrLab/fqrjx/)

What’s this about?  
Smart doorbells are everywhere—Amazon Ring, Google Nest, etc. — but are they really smart? And what are the privacy consequences of these always-on, cloud-connected devices?

In this hands-on workshop, we’ll explore the social and privacy impact of commercial smart doorbells. Then we’ll dive into building our very own privacy-conscious smart doorbell using a Raspberry Pi with camera, basic electronics, and open-source software.

What you’ll learn:

-   The legal & ethical issues of smart surveillance
-   How to build a DIY smart doorbell using Raspberry Pi
-   How to integrate Telegram and Jitsi for private video calls

How it works:  
We’ll guide you step-by-step in building a prototype. All materials are provided during the workshop. Afterwards, you can choose to purchase your own kit (€125–151, depending on configuration) to continue building at home.

Who’s behind this?  
This workshop is created by media artist Roos Groothuizen and Dave Borghuis, founder of hackerspace Tkkrlab.

📦 [Reserve your spot now!](https://tickets.tkkrlab.space/TkkrLab/fqrjx/) Limited to 10 participants. All skill levels welcome.

